{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00715",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.92,
      "end_seconds": 15.87,
      "duration_seconds": 14.95,
      "text": "Hello, doctor! I've come for my heart scan results, the echo. I've been worried sick, to be honest, and I told my sister I'd ring her straight after."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.87,
      "end_seconds": 27.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.38,
      "text": "Let's put your mind at rest as much as we can. First, remind me what's been happening? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.7,
      "end_seconds": 38.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.91,
      "text": "Palpitations, mostly. My heart flutters, like a bird in my chest, a few times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.13,
      "end_seconds": 43.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "And anything else along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.4,
      "end_seconds": 54.1,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "Breathless, when I climb the stairs at work. Third floor, no lift. And a bit dizzy sometimes, when it happens."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.71,
      "end_seconds": 58.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Any chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.53,
      "end_seconds": 63.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "No pain. Thank God."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.17,
      "end_seconds": 66.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Any fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.8,
      "end_seconds": 71.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Never fainted, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.5,
      "end_seconds": 87.67,
      "duration_seconds": 15.17,
      "text": "Okay. Your echocardiogram showed that your heart muscle is pumping normally. But one of the valves, the mitral valve, bulges back a little when it closes. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.77,
      "end_seconds": 91.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Bulges? Is that bad? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.11,
      "end_seconds": 102.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "It's called mitral valve prolapse, and it's common, especially in young women. Usually harmless. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.44,
      "end_seconds": 105.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Usually? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.46,
      "end_seconds": 117.62,
      "duration_seconds": 10.16,
      "text": "In most people it never causes trouble. The palpitations you describe can go with it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.12,
      "end_seconds": 121.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Okay. Phew. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.6,
      "end_seconds": 133.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Let me examine you, to make sure it matches the scan. Pulse and pressure first. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.16,
      "end_seconds": 137.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Of course. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.08,
      "end_seconds": 163.36,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "Pulse 84, blood pressure 112 over 70, temperature 36.7, oxygen 99 percent, respiratory rate 14."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.59,
      "end_seconds": 168.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Is that normal? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.48,
      "end_seconds": 177.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Completely normal. Breathe for me, I'm listening to your heart. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.26,
      "end_seconds": 201.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Is it making a noise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.43,
      "end_seconds": 215.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.96,
      "text": "There's a click in mid-beat, which is the valve, and no murmur. Your lungs are clear, and there's no swelling of your ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.55,
      "end_seconds": 219.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "So it all fits? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.29,
      "end_seconds": 230.88,
      "duration_seconds": 9.59,
      "text": "It does. I'd say what you're feeling is most likely due to the mitral valve prolapse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.49,
      "end_seconds": 236.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "What do I do about it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.17,
      "end_seconds": 251.84,
      "duration_seconds": 13.67,
      "text": "Mostly nothing. Cut down on caffeine, and keep hydrated. But I'd like to be sure the palpitations are benign, so I'd like to arrange a 48-hour heart rhythm monitor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.06,
      "end_seconds": 257.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "The little box I wear? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.25,
      "end_seconds": 269.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.43,
      "text": "Exactly. You wear it, press a button when you feel a flutter, and send it back. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.87,
      "end_seconds": 272.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Easy. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.35,
      "end_seconds": 282.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks, when the monitor results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.82,
      "end_seconds": 291.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "Four weeks. Good. Can I tell my sister it's not serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.07,
      "end_seconds": 299.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Tell her it's common, usually harmless, and being looked after. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.02,
      "end_seconds": 305.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Brilliant. Thank you so much. ~"
    }
  ]
}
